1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,893
An offline-first teacher tool for rural primary schools. Parents use ordinary SMS. Pupils have no account or app.

2
00:00:13,893 --> 00:00:23,831
English, Hausa, Yoruba or Igbo. Non-English interface strings are drafts and fall back to English until native review.

3
00:00:23,831 --> 00:00:36,008
A synthetic teacher signs in with a test phone number. Firestore loads a synthetic workspace. SMS stays mocked.

4
00:00:36,008 --> 00:00:43,621
Today's classes, pending sync, parent messages and quick actions in one calm dashboard.

5
00:00:43,621 --> 00:00:50,630
A teacher can manage more than one class, open a roster, add a class or add a pupil locally.

6
00:00:50,630 --> 00:01:05,042
Only absent pupils create an immediate notification job after server acceptance. Present and late do not.

7
00:01:05,042 --> 00:01:13,886
A saved 5E lesson opens offline. It is a teacher-authored scaffold, not a claim of full NERDC coverage.

8
00:01:13,886 --> 00:01:34,022
On-device Nano is unavailable on this emulator; the SDK falls back to cloud AI and reports Source: Cloud Gemini. Curated strategies remain offline.

9
00:01:34,022 --> 00:01:43,271
In this preview the SMS adapter is mocked, so nothing leaves the device.

10
00:01:43,271 --> 00:01:52,694
A teacher replies from Tiny. Provider acceptance is not the same as delivery.

11
00:01:52,694 --> 00:02:06,706
Link a guardian endpoint, verify it in person and record opt-in. A shared endpoint is reused for siblings.

12
00:02:06,706 --> 00:02:26,642
Remaining gates: App Distribution, App Check enforcement/Play Integrity, native translation review and a supported on-device AI device.
